The cannot find or open error happens because your terminal is currently looking in your Home (~) folder, but your files are likely sitting inside your Downloads directory.
Let's navigate to the right folder first and then run the unzip command.
------------------------------
## 🛠️ Fix and Extract

   1. Change directory to where your files are:
   
   cd ~/Downloads
   
   (If you put them somewhere else, replace ~/Downloads with that folder path).
   2. Verify the file is visible:
   
   ls | grep Tecno
   
   You should see Tecno-Spark-8-KG6k-H6218MNOP-R-GL-230912V614-Flash-File-RMM.zip pop up in green or white text.
   3. Run the extraction command again:
   
   unzip Tecno-Spark-8-KG6k-H6218MNOP-R-GL-230912V614-Flash-File-RMM.zip -d Tecno_Firmware
   
   
------------------------------
